            <ArticleTitle>N-Heterocyclic carbene-catalyzed sulfa-Michael addition of enals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13129-13132</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07269d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient N-heterocyclic carbene (NHC) catalyzed sulfa-Michael addition (SMA) between enals and thiols has been developed. Under the catalysis of 10 mol% stable free carbene IPr and with 20 mol% hexafluoroisopropanol (HFIP) as an additive, enals react with a variety of thiols to afford the SMA adducts in 54-98% yields. In this process, the free carbene preferentially interacts with thiols through hydrogen-bonding and no NHC-catalyzed extended Umpolung transformations were observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
